==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Oni Hayabusa''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Akuma Hayabusa''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
In all of his forms, Hayabusa presents himself as a midrange rusher that utilizes Long Distance attacks. These attacks are another efficient advantage to Hayabusa, allowing him to have wide area coverage and use stepping stones to hit threats that might normally outrange him. While it gives him a blind spot, which results in him having an inner range of only 115, his 7 Knockbacks, another advantage that helps with survivability, help circumvent this. However, this blind spot still hurts his potential against melee threats, though he is by no means useless against them. Another issue is that due to his fast speed and lack of full backswing, Hayabusa is prone to speed-clipping unless he is in his True Form with a maxed Attack Frequency Ultra Talent, forcing you to be careful with Cat Cannon and Knockback unit usage.

His aforementioned blind spot means that this unit can be stacked against melees that can be easily controlled like [[Bore]]. Since all forms of Hayabusa have high speed, it is recommended to either protect him with fast-moving meatshields ([[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Cat]]/[[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Crazed Tank Cat]]), or spawn him after you have a good unit line built up.

Hayabusa is also part of one of the most efficient Speed [[Cat Combo]]s in the game: [[Enter The Ninja (Combo)|Enter The Ninja]]. By simply pairing Hayabusa with [[Ninja Cat (Special Cat)|Ninja Cat]], you can get a Medium Speed Boost. This is a great deal for just two cats. Some might notice a distinctive potential for enticing power: Ninja Cat is also part of the [[Cool Japan (Combo)|Cool Japan Combo]], which means that with [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Sushi Cat]] + [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Sumo Cat]] + [[Samurai Cat (Special Cat)|Samurai Cat]] + Ninja Cat + Hayabusa, you can get both the medium Attack and Speed [[Cat Combo]]s for just 5 slots.

==='''Normal Form'''===
Hayabusa's first form has poor general stats. This is because of his niche as a devastating Critical hitter. He is a considerable offense against [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies, as his Critical chance is solid and his Long Distance allows him to wipe out a huge swarm of [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal enemies]], vastly outperforming many other [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critters]] who may just hit one or two and completely miss the dangerous Metals. In fact, he could use peons like Metal Doge as a stepping stone to hit stronger Metal enemies behind. However, almost all Metals are melee attackers, so the likes of [[Super Metal Hippoe]] and [[Metal One Horn]] can invade his blind spot. Preventing this can be done so by a steady stream of meatshields. Hayabusa also works well in tandem with [[Marauder Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Paladin Cat]], since the former can attack Metal units at a distance, while the latter defeats the Metal enemies that reach to blind spot (if he Crits). If you additionally have [[Princess Kaguya (Uber Rare Cat)|Princess Kaguya]] or other good [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal]] stallers, like the Cats gained from the [[:Category:Cyclone Stages|Cyclone Stages]], you will likely never have problems with Metal enemies ever again.

==='''Evolved Form'''===
Oni Hayabusa gains more general stats and switches to a 50% chance to Knockback and Slow Aliens. Thanks to his pierce, he catches all targets, preventing him from pushing enemies into the range of backliners unless untargeted. Oni Hayabusa is also a strong option to control Alien pushers like [[Nimoy Bore]] and [[Cyberhorn]]. However, keep in mind that many Aliens, such as Maawth and [[I.M. Phace]], naturally outrange him. You should take full advantage of stepping stones to mitigate the damage he takes in most situations, as well as hit backliners more consistently.

Oni Hayabusa forms a powerful combination with [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]. He can stall Aliens initially, allowing your Seafarer stack to slowly build up; they will then return the favor by perma-Freezing Aliens and guarding his blind spot. Oni Hayabusa is therefore very useful throughout [[Into the Future]] and many of the [[Cats of the Cosmos]] stages where he can be deployed.

==='''True Form'''===
Akuma Hayabusa becomes a very effective [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]] crowd-controller, being able to Knockback bulky Zombies like [[Lord Gravey]] or prevent annoying ones from burrowing (e.g., [[Zory]], [[Zir Zeal]], [[Zang Roo]]) should his Knockback and Slow abilities activate. With his Long Distance, he can help clear big chunks of peons while still being able to take on much bulkier Zombies such as [[Zyclone]].

This is where his blind spot should come to bite him the most. Zombies have aggressive melee pushers and abuse Burrow to cut off your meatshield flow and intercept ranged attackers who cannot retaliate. Thankfully, his aforementioned 7 Knockbacks help alleviate this flaw. Note that Hayabusa also struggles with longer-ranged Zombies like [[Cadaver Bear]] and [[Zamelle]].

Akuma Hayabusa therefore has strong usage in certain Zombie-dominant stages, such as [[The Haunted 1LDK]] and [[Heavenly Tower/Floor 27|Floor 27]] of the [[Heavenly Tower]], where he is able to push [[Lord Gravey]] and [[Miss Haka]] all the way back behind the enemy base and keep them there with support.

==='''Talents'''===
'''[[Shield Piercing]]''' should optimally be unlocked first. At Lv.10, Shield Piercing has a 40% activation, which is quite nice given Akuma Hayabusa's Long Distance reach and decently quick attack rate. Granted, the Shield Piercing Talent is so useful that it should be unlocked well before '''Target [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]''', being nigh-required to make his abilities work against Shielded Aku. His standing range allows him to reach [[Fallen Bear]], with Long Distance even putting [[Le'Behemoth]] and [[Lord of Ruin Jagando]] within his effective range.

'''Target [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]]''' is similarly useful in order to take full advantage of his Knockback and Slow abilities against them. This is great if you don't have any better anti-Aku crowd-controllers, especially for late-stage Aku Realms where they become a near-necessity. However, he lacks the bulk necessary to tank the punishment that comes with that role a lot of the time, making it a bit redundant if you already have more consistent options.

'''[[Special Abilities#Resist|Resist Curse]]''' is only ever situational at best and not really worth the NP. While there are a great deal of Relic/Aku stages in the late-gate, the best answer to avoid getting Cursed is to not let him get hit in the first place. Additionally, Curse will disable Knockback/Slow, but doesn't affect Shield Piercing or Zombie Killer, meaning his use isn't hampered much anyway.

'''Attack Buff''' and '''Hp Buff''' are not high-priority pre-Ultra Talents. Akuma Hayabusa does have decent stats for a Long-Distance rusher, but they are not worth boosting with Talents. If anything, [[Catseye]]s should be more than enough. This obviously changes with Ultra Talent investment, once his DPS and HP start playing more of a pivotal role in his overall performance.

==='''Ultra Talents'''===
Akuma Hayabusa's Ultra Talents help transform him into the ultimate anti-Aku assassin, and even a strong generalist.

'''Attack Frequency Up''' doubles his attack rate, giving his Slow a 100% uptime (should it activate) while doubling his DPS, now being similar to a Strengthened [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]], making him a strong midranged rusher even for general use. Not only that, it makes his Shield Piercing proc more consistent, vastly improving his matchups against Shielded Aku. Furthermore, he also ditches the attack cooldown and becomes a rebound unit, making it much easier to pair Hayabusa with Knockback procs.

'''[[Strong Against]]''' shifts his role into a more offensive-oriented DPS, with crowd-controlling capabilities on the side. Combined with Attack Frequency Up, he has ''22,800 DPS against Akus'', and ''27,300 DPS against Zombies''. These numbers trump even some dedicated nukers for these traits like [[White Knight Cyclops (Uber Rare Cat)|Demon Knight Kyklops]] and [[Mighty Aethur Ltd. (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Atlantis Logistix]] at equal levels. This is without even mentioning the fact that it doubles his effective HP to ''176,000 VS. Aku'' and ''220,000 VS. Zombie'', which paired with his 7 Knockbacks, allows him to stick around for a long time, especially for rusher standards.

Finally, '''[[Immune to Surge|Surge Immunity]]''' is mainly a safeguard against Akus and their Death Surges, which is simply neat to have, and makes him a more complete anti-Aku unit. It improves matchups against [[Medu-san]], among other untargeted Surgers like [[Raynard]] and the [[Surge Base (Enemy Base)|Surge Base]].

However, training this ninja to reach such levels of performance requires an absurd NP cost. Most of his Talents are pivotal to achieving optimal performance, and together it'll cost you around 1,210 NP for everything outside of Curse Resist. Therefore, these Ultra Talents are only advised if you truly lack the firepower needed to deal with Akus/Zombies, whether in the form of Ubers or otherwise.

==='''Orb'''===
Strong VS Orbs against Aku or Zombies after unlocking the required Ultra Talent. Berserker Orb can also be used due to his fast attack rate and Long Distance attacks.

