==Trivia==
*Hayabusa gained [[Immune to Slow]] in [[Version 5.3 Update|Version 5.3]].
*Hayabusa's name may be a reference to the main character of the ''[[wikipedia:Ninja Gaiden|Ninja Gaiden]]'' series, Ryu Hayabusa.
*An ''[[wikipedia:Oni|oni]]'' is a demon-like ''[[wikipedia:Yōkai|yōkai]]'' in Japanese folklore, while ''akuma'' (悪魔) is one of the Japanese words for "demon" or "devil" (distinct from ''oni'').
**''Akuma'' is also the Japanese name of the [[:Category:Aku Enemies|Aku]] trait, but this is most likely a coincidence, as Akuma Hayabusa's Japanese name does not contain the word ''akuma''.
*Oni Hayabusa's blade and blue flames may be a reference to Rin Okumura's Kurikara from the ''[[wikipedia:Blue Exorcist|Blue Exorcist]]'' manga and anime series.
*The character that appears just after Oni Hayabusa's attack is the kanji for "slash". This can be seen on frame 34 and 35 of his attack animation.
*Oni Hayabusa's design and attack animation may be a reference to Raiden and his Zandatsu technique from ''[[wikipedia:Metal Gear Rising: Revengeance|Metal Gear Rising: Revengeance]]''.
*Hayabusa is the only [[Justice Strikes Back! Dark Heroes (Gacha Event)|Dark Hero]] whose stats seemingly change between Normal and Evolved Form (as non-[[Critical Hit]]s only inflict 1 damage to Metal enemies, meaning his effective anti-Metal damage is still the same), and is also the only Dark Hero whose Normal Form has no [[:Category:Anti-Alien Cats|anti-Alien]] abilities.
*[[Sakura Sonic (Uber Rare Cat)|Sakura Sonic]] seems to be related to Hayabusa. Both are [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal]], specialists with similarities in their attack animations, both hail from a ninja clan who opposes evil, the first lines of their Normal Forms' Japanese descriptions are nearly identical, their swords are both described as "swords of exorcism" (退魔の刀 ''taima no katana''), and the Japanese names of Oni Hayabusa and Sacred Blade Sakura both contain 天誅 ''tenchū'' ("Heaven's punishment" or "divine retribution"). Furthermore, the kanji 隼 in Sakura's Japanese surname (風隼, ''Kazehaya'') is pronounced ''hayabusa'' on its own.
*Akuma Hayabusa and God-Emperor Vars are the only Cats with Attack Frequency Up Talents to decrease time between attacks by parts of a frame.

